      "id": "JAC-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The inverse-character partner of a Jacobi sum",
      "anchor": "inputs-jacobi-divisibility",
      "statement": "For multiplicative characters χ,φ on F_p with values in a characteristic-zero integral domain, if χ,φ and χφ are all nontrivial, the product J(χ,φ)J(χ⁻¹,φ⁻¹) equals p in the domain. Thus J(χ,φ) divides p and is nonzero.",
      "hypotheses": "p prime, R a commutative characteristic-zero integral domain, characters zero at zero and nonzero character values units. Mathlib proves the field identity for a finite source field and target field of different characteristic. It extends the target to obtain a primitive additive character; the two factor identities descend through injective ring maps.",
