      "correspondence": "xJac_one verifies the three nontrivialities for each residue pair; xJac selects exponents 1,j and computes the product of their principal ideals via xJac_span. For p=7, J(χ,χ)=2+3ω² is the factor at the prime ω↦2, while J(χ⁻¹,χ⁻¹)=2+3ω is the factor at ω↦4. This elementary calculation demonstrates the divisor direction and complementary prime orders. No claim that the product over all j itself divides p.",
