  "outstanding": [
    "Finite-field character orthogonality and existence of a primitive additive character after adjoining roots of unity are library inputs; the proof here opens the two character sum manipulations that use them.",
    "CRL-01–02 reconstruct the integral character lift and complete splitting at the chosen degree-one prime. The explicit residue carry test and ideal class change appear in CYE-01–04. Existence of a degree-one prime in a prescribed ideal class uses a separate theorem.",
    "The divisibility supplies one local exponent calculation in the reciprocity argument. Character-component length bounds also use the primitive-character arithmetic and Poitou–Tate reciprocity of REC-01–03/MIN-02. The Bernoulli denominator clearing in MBF-01 is independent."
  ],
  "review_scope": "In-archive applications and the directly called, pinned Mathlib proof. Arithmetic examples illustrate a single Jacobi factor, separate from the subsequent Bernoulli denominator or Kummer length statements."
}
